What are Speciality Pumps?
Speciality Pumps are precision-engineered machines designed to handle demanding fluid transfer applications where standard pumps fail. These workhorses of industrial processes transfer mechanical energy to move challenging media including corrosive chemicals, high-temperature oils, abrasive slurries, and ultra-pure liquids. Unlike conventional pumps, they feature specialized materials and designs to withstand extreme operating conditions across industries.
The market encompasses four primary pump types:
•	Centrifugal Pumps - Dominant in water treatment and chemical processing
•	Reciprocating Pumps - Preferred for high-pressure oil & gas applications
•	Rotary Pumps - Ideal for viscous fluid handling
•	Diaphragm Pumps - Critical for leak-proof chemical transfer
